winewayland: accept normal compositor size hints after initial configure

PaperWM programmatic resizes do not carry MAXIMIZED/RESIZING/TILED states.
The normal window is resizable, but the driver discarded both dimensions.
Preserve initial-configure and fixed-size behavior; keep application constraints.
Wine-derived change: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -568,9 +568,12 @@
     memset(&surface->requested, 0, sizeof(surface->requested));
 
     state = surface->processing.state;
-    /* Ignore size hints if we don't have a state that requires strict
-     * size adherence, in order to avoid spurious resizes. */
-    if (state)
+    /* A window manager may resize a normal window without marking it tiled
+     * or interactively resizing (e.g. PaperWM move_resize_frame). Once the
+     * initial configure is acknowledged, respect such hints for resizable
+     * windows. Keep initial placement and fixed-size dialogs unchanged, and
+     * retain the application's normal WM_WINDOWPOSCHANGING constraints. */
+    if (state || (surface->current.serial && surface->window.resizeable))
     {
         width = surface->processing.rect.right - surface->processing.rect.left;
         height = surface->processing.rect.bottom - surface->processing.rect.top;
